p.m:
\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}
   \frac{1}{6} + \frac{7}{12}
        \amp = \frac{2}{12} + \frac{7}{12} \\
        \amp = \frac{2 + 7}{12} \\
        \amp = \frac{9}{12} \amp  \hbox{We can reduce this by dividing 3 into both the numerator and the denominator.}\\
        \amp = \frac{3}{4}
\end{aligned}
    }
